AIM OF PROGRAM
This program has been developed to allow quick calculation between input and
output ranges of industrial instrumentation equipment, for calibration and repair work. The
program can deal with 1 input ~ 1 output or 1 input ~ 2 output.
For example:
To work out the relevant values for a 2 output loop for a reservoir level of 4.56
metres in a range of 5.475 metres, where the first output from the level transducer
is ranged 4-20 mA and the second output is a bargraph indicator ranged 0-100%.




Install and start up the program

With the arrow keys, select 2 output and press Enter.
At the dialog box enter 0 for input range low limit and press Enter.
Likewise select 5.475 for the input high range.
Select 4 and 20 for the first output range low and high limits.
Select 0 and 100 for the second ouput range low and high limits.
At the "Enter Actual Input Value" prompt, enter 4.56.
The input and output ranges are then displayed on the screen along with the
correct outputs at the respective points.





The output values can be used to test outputs from equipment and
determine if the output is correct or that particular piece of equipment requires
attention.
To account for a fluctuating input value, while the answer is being displayed on
screen, the input can be modified up and down in increments of 1% of input full
range using the up and down arrows on the keyboard.
Press enter for options:
Choose either:
Quit -> Back to System Screen
Reselect Input ->  Use Same Ranges but different Input
Repeat from Start -> Go back to Title Page.
Note: When using the one output facility, an extra option is included at this point.
The input range  and output range can be swapped, keeping the same actual input
value, to account for human error in inputting ranges.- This does happen!